@31 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to take part in an experiment with him. Are you interested?~
@32 = ~Who is your master?~
@33 = ~What kind of experiment?~
@34 = ~My master's name is Telim'Gar.~
@35 = ~An experiment concerning the intrinsic power possessed by all those capable of overcoming challenges.~
@36 = ~All right, and what kind of experiment is it?~
@37 = ~Very well. How can I help?~
@38 = ~Without more information, I'll pass. Goodbye.~
@39 = ~If you wish to help the master, you must first prove your power by completing the challenges.~
@310 = ~What challenges?~
@311 = ~I offer the challenges; you choose. Each challenge sends you "elsewhere," and you must return with a magical rune as proof of your victory.~
@312 = ~A magical rune?~
@313 = ~Yes, a magical rune.~
@314 = ~All right. Show me your challenges, golem.~
@315 = ~In that case, no thanks. I'm leaving.~
@316 = ~The Dump.~
@317 = ~The Silent Necropolis.~
@318 = ~The Plant Labyrinth.~
@319 = ~The Steel Tombs.~
@320 = ~The Maze.~
@321 = ~Antimaginium.~
@322 = ~The Furnace.~
@323 = ~The Tomb of the Great Wyrm.~
@324 = ~The Playroom of the Evil.~
@325 = ~The Pocket of Normality.~
@326 = ~The Library.~
@327 = ~That's it? No details, no explanations?~
@328 = ~Explanations: already given. Details: none.~
@329 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to take part in an experiment with him. You cheated by leaving a challenge without the corresponding rune. The master knows this and refuses to receive you.~
@330 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to take part in an experiment with him. You have proven your power. You may meet the master.~
@331 = ~The Forge.~
@332 = ~Which challenge do you want to take on?~
@333 = ~Actually, I'll come back later.~
@334 = ~Never mind. Show me the challenges I still have left to attempt.~
@335 = ~Then I'm leaving.~
@336 = ~All right, let's go.~
@337 = ~Maybe later.~
@338 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to take part in an experiment with him. You have defeated the master, so you will have to wait a decade for him to rebuild his challenges.~
@339 = ~Hello. My master is looking for powerful adventurers like you to take part in an experiment with him. You have begun the experiment. Would you like to continue?~
@340 = ~Yes. Show me the challenges I still have left to attempt.~
@341 = ~What are the Library, the Gallery of Anomalies, and the Pasture?~
@342 = ~*The golem stares at you without reacting for a few seconds before answering.* You do not have access to the Library.~
@343 = ~All right, but what about the Gallery of Anomalies and the Pasture?~
@344 = ~I do not have that information.~